     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The crown can be reached three ways: through h4_3:reach, h4_2:reach or h4_1:escalate. h4_3 and h4_2 both depend only on h3_2:escalate, and h3_2 is reachable from h2_0:escalate or from h2_3:access. h4_1 is an AND step that needs both h3_3:escalate (which comes from h2_0) and h2_2:access. Blocking h3_2 cuts off h4_2 and h4_3. Also blocking h2_2 (or h3_3) stops h4_1, so a set of 2 works. No single block is enough: blocking h3_2 leaves h4_1 open, and blocking h2_0 leaves h3_2 reachable through h2_3. Each other single candidate also leaves at least one path open.\"}"
    }
